WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.752 --> 00:00:17.114
moon was going down when Mowgli reached the wolves' cave.

2
00:00:17.915 --> 00:00:20.036
He was carrying Shere Khan's hide.

3
00:00:20.056 --> 00:00:24.179
"Mowgli?" Mother's eyes glowed.

4
00:00:28.502 --> 00:00:30.804
all knew you'd hunt Shere Khan one day.

5
00:00:31.508 --> 00:00:32.169
Well done!"

6
00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:35.972
A deep voice came from some shrubs.

7
00:00:36.512 --> 00:00:37.753
"Well done indeed!"

8
00:00:39.175 --> 00:00:40.716
Bagheera ran toward them.

9
00:00:40.736 --> 00:00:45.620
"Mowgli, the jungle has been lonely without you."

10
00:00:50.744 --> 00:00:54.788
Soon the group of friends climbed up the hill to Council Rock.

11
00:01:00.156 --> 00:01:04.799
Mowgli spread the hide out on the flat stone at the top of Council Rock.

12
00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:11.022
As the wolves gathered, Mowgli beckoned Akela to lie on the hide.

13
00:01:18.346 --> 00:01:19.867
well, oh, wolves!"

14
00:01:20.367 --> 00:01:21.828
Akela called loudly.

15
00:01:22.688 --> 00:01:25.870
The wolf pack had been without a leader for a while now.

16
00:01:26.771 --> 00:01:29.212
Many of the wolves were thin and hungry.

17
00:01:30.192 --> 00:01:31.853
Some were sick or wounded.

18
00:01:32.713 --> 00:01:35.394
Out of habit, they answered Akela's call.

19
00:01:37.074 --> 00:01:41.675
They stared in surprise when they saw the tiger's striped hide on the rock.

20
00:01:44.396 --> 00:01:45.396
A few gasped.

21
00:01:46.117 --> 00:01:47.317
"Shere Khan!"

22
00:01:48.057 --> 00:01:49.398
They looked toward Mowgli.

23
00:01:49.418 --> 00:01:53.999
"I have kept my word," the boy said proudly.

24
00:01:55.199 --> 00:01:56.640
A skinny wolf howled.

25
00:01:58.892 --> 00:02:01.514
"Please, Akela, lead our pack again.

26
00:02:01.874 --> 00:02:05.476
We are hungry and tired of living without laws."

27
00:02:06.877 --> 00:02:09.078
Bagheera grunted near Mowgli's ear.

28
00:02:09.098 --> 00:02:12.680
"This is what the wolves say now.

29
00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:17.122
When they are well-fed again, they will not listen to Akela or anyone."

30
00:02:18.323 --> 00:02:19.204
Mowgli nodded.

31
00:02:20.204 --> 00:02:22.465
He didn't trust these wolves either.

32
00:02:24.447 --> 00:02:26.688
Later Mowgli returned to the cave.

33
00:02:27.808 --> 00:02:32.691
He slept for a day and a night, his heart feeling oddly heavy.

34
00:02:36.974 --> 00:02:39.375
When he awoke, Akela was visiting.

35
00:02:40.376 --> 00:02:42.117
So were Baloo and Bagheera.

36
00:02:43.117 --> 00:02:47.820
Everyone wanted to hear the story about the victory over Shere Khan again.

37
00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:54.044
"Akela and Gray Brother were a big help," Mowgli said.

38
00:02:55.444 --> 00:02:58.606
"You should have seen the buffalo pouring down the ravine!"

39
00:02:58.626 --> 00:03:03.929
"Well, I'm glad that I didn't see the humans throwing stones at you."

40
00:03:04.369 --> 00:03:05.470
Mother Wolf frowned.

41
00:03:05.490 --> 00:03:07.971
"I would have hunted all of them.

42
00:03:08.652 --> 00:03:11.333
Except for the kind woman who took care of you."

43
00:03:15.956 --> 00:03:18.677
down, Mother," Father Wolf said lazily.

44
00:03:18.697 --> 00:03:21.119
"Mowgli has come back again.

45
00:03:21.599 --> 00:03:22.860
What else matters?"

46
00:03:24.124 --> 00:03:26.686
Mowgli lay his head on Mother Wolf's side.

47
00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:34.011
"For my part, I never want to see or hear or smell humans again."

48
00:03:35.152 --> 00:03:37.654
Akela tilted his head to look at Mowgli.

49
00:03:37.674 --> 00:03:41.957
"What if the humans don't leave you alone, Little Brother?"

50
00:03:43.077 --> 00:03:45.079
Gray Brother growled softly.

51
00:03:46.059 --> 00:03:48.982
Bagheera twitched his tail and glanced at Akela.

52
00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:51.263
"What made you say that?"

53
00:03:51.703 --> 00:03:52.224
he asked.

54
00:03:53.496 --> 00:03:58.618
"After last night's council, I went home along the trail," Akela answered.

55
00:03:58.638 --> 00:04:01.279
"I saw Mang the bat.

56
00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:05.941
He told me that the humans' village has been humming like a bees' nest."

57
00:04:07.582 --> 00:04:09.363
"So?" Mowgli shrugged.

58
00:04:09.383 --> 00:04:11.864
"The humans are often busy."

59
00:04:11.884 --> 00:04:17.646
"So, the bat saw the red flower blooming at the village gate.

60
00:04:18.627 --> 00:04:20.968
He also saw some men sitting near it.

61
00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:23.381
They were holding guns."

62
00:04:24.721 --> 00:04:26.682
Akela looked Mowgli in the eye.

63
00:04:26.702 --> 00:04:31.624
"And I believe I smelled a man along our trail this morning."

64
00:04:31.644 --> 00:04:36.306
"They are hunting you, Mowgli," Bagheera said.

65
00:04:36.326 --> 00:04:39.727
"But they threw me out of their pack!"

66
00:04:40.247 --> 00:04:40.988
Mowgli said.

67
00:04:41.008 --> 00:04:44.229
"Why can't they just leave me alone?"

68
00:04:44.249 --> 00:04:49.131
"You're a human, Little Brother," Akela replied softly.

69
00:04:49.151 --> 00:04:51.132
"We are animals.

70
00:04:51.816 --> 00:04:54.319
We cannot explain your kind to you."

71
00:04:55.740 --> 00:04:56.921
Mowgli looked down.

72
00:04:57.862 --> 00:04:59.183
He didn't know what to say.

73
00:04:59.203 --> 00:05:01.285
"What's that?"

74
00:05:01.966 --> 00:05:03.547
Bagheera sprang to his feet.

75
00:05:05.008 --> 00:05:06.029
He sniffed the air.

76
00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:08.071
His body stiffened.

77
00:05:09.092 --> 00:05:13.816
Gray Brother did the same thing, sniffing the wind that was blowing from the right.

78
00:05:13.837 --> 00:05:16.099
"It's a human's scent!"

79
00:05:16.439 --> 00:05:17.220
Bagheera said.
